      "text": "**Project Discovery Walker: Recursively find projects by marker files (not just `.git`)**\n- [ ] Replace `find_git_repos` with `find_projects` walking via `os.walk`, identifying a project as any dir containing `.git` OR a language marker (`package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `setup.py`, `requirements.txt`, `Gemfile`, `Package.swift`, `Makefile.PL`, `cpanfile`, `Makefile`, `configure`, `CMakeLists.txt`, `DESCRIPTION`)\n- [ ] Stop descending once a project root is identified (don't double-count subprojects)\n- [ ] Hardcode an excluded-dir list (`node_modules`, `__pycache__`, `.venv`, `venv`, `target`, `build`, `dist`, `vendor`, `.mypy_cache`, `.pytest_cache`, `.ruff_cache`); CSV-loading is a follow-up\n- [ ] Update `emit_markdown` to gracefully degrade for non-git projects (skip `git` tag, omit Remote bullet, render \"(non-git project)\" timestamp)\n- [ ] Smoke test on `~/bin/` (still 14 git repos) plus a constructed mixed tree\n\n`TODO.md:L25`",
